  "problem": "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},\u2026,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[2,6]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},\u2026,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[4,6]$\n\nCalculate  ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})\u0394{x}_{i}\u0394{y}_{j},$ where $\u0394{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $\u0394{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})\u0394{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\u0394{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\u0394{y}_{j}$ is just the length of the interval $[4,6].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\u0394{y}_{j}=6-4=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $i,$ we can evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})\u0394{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})\u0394{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})\u0394{x}_{2}+\u22ef+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})\u0394{x}_{n} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+\u22ef+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+\u22ef+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+\u22ef+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={6}^{2}-{2}^{2} \\\\  & =32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})\u0394{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\u0394{y}_{j}=32\\cdot 2=64.\n$$",
